  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "A hot iron bar is placed in an ice bath. The initial temperature of the bar is $100^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$. After 20 seconds, the temperature of the bar is $60^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$. The temperature of the bar is decaying exponentially to $0^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p27-q11-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Determine the temperature of the bar after 50 seconds, correct to the nearest degree.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$28^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$",
          "worked": "Let $T(t)$ be the temperature in degrees Celsius after $t$ seconds. The temperature is multiplied by $\\frac{60}{100}=\\frac35$ every 20 seconds, so\n$$\\begin{align*}T(t)&=100\\left(\\frac35\\right)^{t/20}\\\\T(50)&=100\\left(\\frac35\\right)^{50/20}\\\\T(50)&\\approx27.88548.\\end{align*}$$\nThe temperature is $28^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$ to the nearest degree.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q11-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Determine how long it will take for the temperature of the bar to be $20^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$, correct to the nearest second.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p27-q11-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "63 seconds.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p27-q11-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use logarithms to solve ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\left(\\frac35\\right)^{t/20}=\\frac15",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Using $T(t)=100\\left(\\frac35\\right)^{t/20}$,\n$$\\begin{align*}100\\left(\\frac35\\right)^{t/20}&=20\\\\\\left(\\frac35\\right)^{t/20}&=\\frac15\\\\\\log_{10}\\left(\\left(\\frac35\\right)^{t/20}\\right)&=\\log_{10}\\frac15\\\\\\frac{t}{20}\\log_{10}\\frac35&=\\log_{10}\\frac15\\\\t&=\\frac{20\\log_{10}(1/5)}{\\log_{10}(3/5)}\\\\t&\\approx63.01320.\\end{align*}$$\nIt takes 63 seconds to the nearest second.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      }
    ]
  },
